    "narrative": "The standout play on today\u2019s board is **Corbin Carroll**, whose 87.14 efficiency score cements him as the cornerstone of our lineup. He benefits from a favorable matchup against Adams and is maximized by his elite sprint speed in a park environment that amplifies his upside. Close behind is **Mickey Moniak** (75.75), who presents a significant platoon advantage against the right-handed Kelly; his 14% boost from the platoon and favorable park conditions make him an essential start despite hitting lower in the order. Similarly, **James Wood** (74.56) is a high-conviction play today; while he faces the left-handed Valdez, his elite .408 xwOBA and the 10% boost afforded by the lead-off spot outweigh the neutral handedness, and the slow delivery of the opposing staff keeps his stolen base potential firmly in play.\n\nOur roster management remains focused on maximizing category density in the face of varying SP skill levels. **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10) and **Josh Naylor** (69.73) provide reliable offensive floors, while **Austin Riley** (66.96) is a vital start at 3B, bolstered by a 19% edge against a favorable SP profile and a slight uptick in SB probability due to the opponent\u2019s slow delivery. On the bench, **Griffin Conine** (48.73) fell just short of the starting rotation. While his platoon edge against Gausman was appealing, the projected efficiency of our starting outfield\u2014particularly the speed profiles of **Jose Caballero** and **Corbin Carroll**\u2014simply proved too valuable for a 5x5 Roto build that prioritizes stolen bases as the scarcest commodity.\n\nManagers should monitor **Trevor Story** and **Brice Turang** closely; both carry risks related to elite catchers and defensive metrics that temper their overall efficiency scores. While **Brice Turang** maintains a 60.47, the 2% drag from the opposing battery represents a non-negligible headwind. We are currently navigating a depleted bench as we monitor the health of **Tyler Soderstrom**, who remains sidelined on the IL. With **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Griffin Conine** all providing depth, we have the necessary pivots if late-breaking weather or lineup changes necessitate a shift, but for today, we are leaning into the high-upside speed threats of **James Wood** and **Corbin Carroll** to separate us from the pack.",
